reason = "Situation 2. The obligation `value-is-L` is delivered nowhere: Probe615.agda binds no term of that name and the witness meter reports `missing exit=42`, 1 UNRESOLVED of 1, probe_red=False. What settles it is the task's own proof, which its brief funded in advance. The brief said: if ValueIsL turns out to need TransferL, say so and stop, because that would mean the factorization does not split the way its author thought. It does need it. The stop statement's own title is 'the recovered second factor needs TransferL, the factorization does not split paid from unpaid'. TransferL is an ambient-to-inner transfer and runs in the direction LJ-1.533 measured as unpaid, 'Code buys ambient. Ambient buys nothing', which is why the brief funded ValueIsL and refused to fund TransferL. So retrying LJ-1.615 is not unlikely to help: the factorization it was built on does not separate a payable factor from an unpayable one, and there is no second route to ValueIsL in that decomposition. The row is parked at attempt_max:sys-lint-accept, a lint failure on the return and not on the mathematics; the mathematical deliverable, the stop, is written and in the tree."
